"""Approximate a dai/dae-related spelling response, not a universal sound rule.

The strongest negatives are isolated 代 and 대. Selected compounds and
related Chinese, Japanese and Roman spellings get weaker responses. A short
text/byte tail recognizes split spellings; document boundaries reset it.
Numbered generations/decades are weaker; party-congress compounds stronger.
Initial whole-syllable spellings are amplified.
Separate rules cover doubled middle dots, an initial Title: field, and
some initial C directives. Small token-specific effects are omitted.
"""
import re
import unicodedata

READS = ()


def step(carry, prefix, upstream):
    doc = prefix.document_ids[-1]
    initial = carry is None or carry[0] != doc
    previous = '' if initial else carry[1]
    raw_tail = b'' if initial else carry[2]
