Its clearest rare peak is Java's 'import static': respond at 'static', less
strongly in source quoted with escaped newlines. Also recognize 'file is part'
license headers, ordinary 'import java', and the words addition and edition.
Repeated middle-dot separators are negative. At document starts, use a coarse
negative bias based on whether the token is a word or punctuation.
These rules capture selected patterns, not most of the activation variance.
