"""layers.1.mlp.down_proj : component 2158, a two-part detector.

1. Year digits (positive). On the last digit of a standalone four-digit year
   such as "in 1997" or "in 201|5", the component is strongly positive. The
   strength depends on the year: 1970-2029 is strongest, 1900s and 2000s are
   a bit weaker, 1800s weaker still. Four-digit runs that sit inside a longer
   number (e.g. "12019") or in maths/code numbers ("-2000") are ignored.

2. Indentation spaces (negative). A lone space token that continues a run of
   ordinary space tokens (code indentation, e.g. the space before a line
   number in a numbered listing or a table cell) is strongly negative.

Everything else is 0. The program reads only the tokens up to the current
position, so it is causal.
"""

READS = ()


def _is_digit(s):
    return len(s) == 1 and s in "0123456789"


def _is_space_run(s):
    return s != "" and set(s) == {" "}


def _year_value(prefix3):
    if prefix3 in ("197", "198", "199", "200", "201", "202"):
        return 2.2
    if prefix3[:2] in ("19", "20"):
        return 1.5
    if prefix3[:2] == "18":
        return 0.9
    return 0.0


